Patch virtio-media 0.0.8 (crates.io copy): per-session MMAP offsets in the V4L2 proxy.

The proxy keyed MMAP buffers by the host V4L2 mem offset and registered that same offset in its MMAP range. Host
offsets are per open file (every session's OUTPUT queue starts at 0, CAPTURE at the same base), so a second
concurrent session on the device (Firefox opens several decoders) registered an occupied offset and the
`.unwrap()` panicked the media worker, which stops the whole VM. Here the proxy hands the guest offsets of its
own (unique across sessions), translates them in every buffer it returns, and an MMAP request only resolves
buffers of the requesting session.

